WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:07.059 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  there is fantastic rich complexity in  the world around us but the beauty and  the cruelty of existence is not  something we can always handle alone  [Music]  that struggle to survive extends beyond  humans and includes all life on the  planet there a seemingly endless  menagerie of creatures to live compete  and sometimes help one another as they  populate the earth even the very  smallest are an important part of this  web of life but how did this come to be  for us to find out let's go back to a  time of ancient competition and see how  a simple prokaryotic cell no more than a  membrane nucleic acids and proteins  evolved a remarkably beneficial  relationship to help it thrive  billions of years ago these early cells  lived in rich waters searching for  energy some cells concealed energy from  molecules directly some of those cells  became energy sources for others while  still other cells evolved the ability to  use sunlight to split water molecules as  an energy source but the pure oxygen  released in this reaction changed the  very atmosphere of the planets and  likely harmed other prokaryotes many  didn't survive but what's this here is  the cell that evolved to use oxygen as a  powerful energy source allowing it to  thrive in this new oxygen-rich  environment but the cells still competed  for survival in a dangerous world then  something remarkable happened a larger  cell engulfed our little oxygen using  cell but this time the little cells  survived inside its host now the smaller  cell could harness energy from oxygen  but this time from the safety of its new  home even more energy than it needed  allowing it to share energy with the  larger whole cell in return the host  cell provided nutrients and safety from  predators this relationship was simply  too good to end over generations the two  cells descendants exchanged DNA and  became dependent on each other for  survival living as one organism in an  evolutionary process called  endosymbiosis this mutually beneficial  relationship only deepened over time  allowing the evolution of what we know  today as the eukaryote with a true  nucleus and organelles that complete  specialized tasks  and what about that little oxygen  consuming cell it evolved into the  mitochondrion which still harnesses most  of the energy in eukaryotic cells in  your own body right now a mitochondrion  can maintain an electric field across  its membrane of 30 million volts per  year a potential that is equal to the  energy released by a bolt of lightning  in the sky this energy supported the  evolution of even more structures in  more diverse combinations changing and  building on one another over time all of  the varied multicellular life on earth  derives from that cooperative  relationship in our ancient past had it  not been for this chance relationship so  long ago life on earth wouldn't exist as  it does today it all began with cells  evolving to cooperate and create new  possibilities for life  [Music]

